From: ucec41188340e8212 at groups.google.com (Yu, Guangchuang)
Date: Fri, 19 Jan 2018 03:14:04 +0000
Subject: Re: what's legend group 0 mean
Message-ID: <gpCn_rSjJ24.Wb2t5A32AgAJ@bioc-ggtree.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <gpCn_rSjJ24.yjGHGYMOBAAJ@bioc-ggtree.groups.google.com>
References: <gpCn_rSjJ24.yjGHGYMOBAAJ@bioc-ggtree.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/bioc-ggtree/c/gpCn_rSjJ24/m/Wb2t5A32AgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The group 0 is reserved for any branches that are not belonging to any groups.

For legend, you can rename it or disable it.

Try :
ggtree(tree, aes(color=group)) + geom_tiplab() +
     scale_color_manual(values=c('black', rainbow_hcl(4)), breaks=names(cls)) + theme(legend.position="right")

It will display the legend without ‘group 0’.
​

